# ── points.md #221: density-threshold experiment. 8x30 (240-cell) clone
# of top_stripped_zone750_v5.v's EXACT structure (same row-buffer fixes
# #180/#186, same witness-cell freeze mechanism) -- ROWS the only changed
# dimension (25->8), COLS unchanged (30), a controlled comparison against
# v5's own 750-cell numbers testing whether overall netlist SIZE itself
# (not local placement congestion, already ruled out by #208's LogicLock
# test) changes Quartus's fitter behavior at some threshold between 25
# cells (#171, 3.36 ALM/cell) and 750 cells (~103 ALM/cell, #207-#211).
# Alan's plan: 25-cell reconfirm -> this 240-cell midpoint -> compare
# against the existing 750-cell numbers -- if ALM/cell inflates somewhere
# in this window, that's a real contender and narrows the threshold. ──
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE ../verilog/unicell_stripped_v1.v
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE ../verilog/cell_wrapper_v2.v
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE ../verilog/cell_command_v1.v
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_FILE ../verilog/top_stripped_zone240_v1.v

